Fixed. The bug was in `CarbonInterval::add()` (src/Carbon/CarbonInterval.php:2182): for intervals created from a date diff, `total*` properties are computed from the stored start/end dates, but mutating units via `add()`/`sub()` left those dates untouched, so totals stayed stale while `forHumans()` (unit-based) was correct.

The fix applies the same delta to the end date (respecting the invert/sign logic) whenever the interval carries `startDate`/`endDate`:

```php
if ($this->startDate && $this->endDate) {
    $delta = clone $interval;
    if ($sign === self::NEGATIVE) {
        $delta->invert = $delta->invert ? 0 : 1;
    }
    $this->endDate = $this->endDate->add($delta);
}
```

Verified: the issue repro now prints `130`, `tests/CarbonInterval/TotalTest.php` passes (including the new `testAlterationAfterDiff`), and the full suite passes except pre-existing, unrelated PHPStan MacroTest failures that also fail without the change.
